  body: "# MA for a participating spouse or civil partner\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source describes
    a separate MA route for a participating wife or civil partner of a self-employed earner and says it does not
    replace the ordinary MA route.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe source uses an expected-confinement boundary
    of 27 July 2014 and separately discusses periods before 18 May 2014. The stated 14-week period must not be replaced
    by the general 39-week maximum. Participation, contribution and other detailed conditions remain unmodelled.\n\
    \n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 62701, PDF page 37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6915b60ebc34c86ce4e6e71b/dmg-ch-62.pdf#page=37).\n\
    - [DMG 62702, PDF page 37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6915b60ebc34c86ce4e6e71b/dmg-ch-62.pdf#page=37).\n\
    - [DMG 62002, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6915b60ebc34c86ce4e6e71b/dmg-ch-62.pdf#page=3).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch62`:
    PDF `5c26aeea45beff88bc30b486b5af521d76c8db81a591a96f8f333285870d6431`; extracted pages `a93501ebcedfbd5cd44cdd7432521274e54a477ee5db81316239e7bdcacdfe6d`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.852961Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6915b60ebc34c86ce4e6e71b/dmg-ch-62.pdf#page=37
