    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The introduction expressly contrasts the special 14-week MA period with the general period.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch62/0003
      quote: "62002 Both SMP and MA are payable for a maximum period of 39 weeks. SMP is paid to the woman by\n\
        her employer; MA is claimed from and paid by DWP. From 1.4.99 decisions on entitlement to SMP are\nmade
        by HMRC. All MA issues are determined by the DM. However, MA is payable for a period of 14\nweeks where
        a woman is a participating wife or civil partner of a S/E earner.\n\n\nNote: From 1.12.14, women whose EWC
        is on or after 5.4.15 can curtail their 39 week MAP (see DMG"
      locator: DMG 62002
